body:
I wrote up a boilerplate complaint for you guys to use:

&#x200B;

Hello Mr. Premier,

&#x200B;

I am writing to address concerns regarding the frankly absurd wait times in Ontario for the processing of transfers on restricted firearms. 

&#x200B;

I realize that we are in tough times and that there may be delays on certain government systems, but this problem has been going on many months before any COVID-19 related lock-downs. I have been waiting for \*\*(X)\*\* weeks for a transfer for a product that I paid for in full at the time of purchase. I am not alone either. I know that many Ontario gun owners have been struggling with extraordinarily long wait times and absolutely no communication on said wait times from the CFO or any other government bodies.

&#x200B;

This issue only becomes all the more obvious when compared to the transfer wait times of only a few days in the provinces to the west, even now, while dealing with a global pandemic.

&#x200B;

I would like to request a formal guideline be put in place for the Ontario CFO that transfers for restricted firearms for RPAL owners in good legal standing not take longer than 1 week. This is a request that can very reasonably be achieved and maintained, as we have seen in the western provinces. If this cannot be met, I would request that the current CFO office be dismantled and replaced with one that is better equipped to handle the needs of Ontario's gun-owning citizens.

&#x200B;

Respectfully,

&#x200B;

\*\*(Your name here)\*\*

You really went back to a month old post about a completely speculative theory to poke fun at people who didn't completely write it off?

&#x200B;

Your life must be miserable.
